 "WHY_PICTURES": "tools/vocabulary.py: a board word \"has to be a word a picture could replace - concrete, or a number or colour\". The guide's words were not chosen that way - the যুক্তবর্ণ table needs an example of ম্ল whether or not anything can be drawn for অম্ল - so guide_levels.py sets only the words listed here, and this is the picture. A word absent from this map is one nothing can show: অবস্থা, নিষ্ঠা, বিভাজ্য, স্নাতক, অর্থ. Emotions count as drawable - the pool already draws রাগ as a cross face - and so do numbers and colours. Proper nouns do not (গঙ্গা, মক্কা, কাশ্মীর), nor does anything a child would read back as a different word: a picture of a farmer is read as চাষী, not as কৃষি."
